@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] managed-github-credential-custody
Managed GitHub clients MUST address only the reviewed broker routes, strip guest
credentials before dispatch and keep github.com as their logical repository host.
The managed-auth marker MUST be public configuration, never a bearer credential.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] managed-github-single-attempt
Managed mutating HTTP requests MUST NOT be retried or followed across redirects.
An ambiguous upstream result MUST remain ambiguous and MUST NOT trigger replay.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] managed-github-pinned-sources
Managed client packages MUST build from hash-pinned upstream sources with the
supplied Nixpkgs Go toolchain. Cross-compilation alone MUST NOT establish guest
runtime qualification or alter an admitted immutable native image identity.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security] managed-lfs-reviewed-release
The managed LFS source tag/hash, package version, vendor label, patch and module
hash MUST identify the same reviewed release independently of Nixpkgs git-lfs.
